WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.118 --> 00:00:23.389
Later that evening Ben was eating dinner with his family.

2
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.285
"How was school today?" Ben's father asked.

3
00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:29.160
"Were monsters getting ready for the pet show?"

4
00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:35.990
"Yes," Ben said. "When I signed up to volunteer, I got to see some cool pets.

5
00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:39.221
The real show takes place tomorrow and Saturday."

6
00:00:39.222 --> 00:00:45.581
He told his family about the obedience, tricks, and best pet competitions.

7
00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:49.573
"I hope you're not shopping for a pet," his mother said.

8
00:00:49.574 --> 00:00:53.380
Ben took another bite of creeploaf and didn't answer.

9
00:00:53.381 --> 00:00:56.836
But his brother Sid's ears had perked up.

10
00:00:56.837 --> 00:00:59.898
"Can we get a pet, Mom? Please?"

11
00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:01.865
His mother looked at Ben.

12
00:01:01.866 --> 00:01:05.626
"Please pass the spoiled eggs, Ben. The slime sauce too."

13
00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:09.454
Ben passed the food as Sid tried another approach.

14
00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:12.208
"Can I at least go to the pet show?" he asked.

15
00:01:12.209 --> 00:01:15.404
"I want to see some cool pets too."

16
00:01:15.405 --> 00:01:18.992
"Maybe we can all go to the show together," Ben's dad suggested.

17
00:01:18.993 --> 00:01:22.565
He put a big pile of fried bat wings on his plate.

18
00:01:22.566 --> 00:01:28.166
"Sid's right. It would be interesting to see the pets—and it could be a fun family outing."

19
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:35.388
Ben's mother shook her head. "I don't know if that's such a good idea."

20
00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:38.348
"I know you don't like dogs, Mom," Ben said.

21
00:01:38.349 --> 00:01:41.005
"But there will be other pets at the show."

22
00:01:41.006 --> 00:01:45.320
She shuddered. "I can't stand most animals.

23
00:01:45.321 --> 00:01:48.064
Uncle Edgar's bird gives me the creeps.

24
00:01:48.065 --> 00:01:56.707
Aunt Petunia's stinkworm makes her house smell terrible, and the neighbors' tarantula is always digging up our backyard!"

25
00:01:56.708 --> 00:01:59.119
Ben's father put down his fork.

26
00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.433
"Maybe Ben, Sid, and I will go to the show," he said.

27
00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.728
"You can stay home, honey."

28
00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:11.309
"You're forgetting something," she said. "Sid is allergic to some animals."

29
00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.908
"It's okay, Mom," Sid said quickly.

30
00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:16.301
"I just break out in green spots.

31
00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.142
Green spots are a little itchy, but they look cool!

32
00:02:19.151 --> 00:02:23.964
I'll put up with hundreds of green spots, if it means we can have a pet."

33
00:02:23.965 --> 00:02:27.903
"Good one, Sid!" Ben thought, glancing hopefully at his mother.

34
00:02:27.904 --> 00:02:30.603
But her lips were tightly pursed.

35
00:02:30.604 --> 00:02:34.204
"We're not getting a pet," she said firmly.

36
00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:39.179
"Right now we are only talking about pets—and the pet show."

37
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.947
"Where we can definitely find a pet that you'll like!" Ben said.

38
00:02:42.948 --> 00:02:47.644
"I'll be at the show all weekend long. It's a great opportunity!"

39
00:02:47.645 --> 00:02:52.316
Sid clapped his hands. "Yeah!"

40
00:02:52.317 --> 00:02:54.575
"Boys, that's not what I said."

41
00:02:54.576 --> 00:03:01.510
Ben's mother closed her eyes and took a deep breath.

42
00:03:01.511 --> 00:03:03.679
Then she opened them again.

43
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.810
"Okay, I'll think about it. But I'm making no promises."

44
00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:10.954
"I can help Ben look at pets at the show," Sid said.

45
00:03:10.955 --> 00:03:15.690
"We'll do a simple test. If I don't get green spots, I'm not allergic."

46
00:03:15.691 --> 00:03:19.807
Their mother tapped a finger on the table. "Hmm . . ."

47
00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:23.600
"We can at least let the boys look around at the show," their father said.

48
00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.019
"There's no harm in that."

49
00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.336
"Please, Mom," Ben pleaded softly.

50
00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.721
"All right," she said at last.

51
00:03:32.722 --> 00:03:36.989
"You two can look." She stared hard at Ben.

52
00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:42.023
"But if Sid starts sneezing or itching a lot, you have to bring him home immediately."

53
00:03:42.024 --> 00:03:44.404
"Bring him home?" Ben repeated.

54
00:03:44.405 --> 00:03:46.527
"Yes," his mother said.

55
00:03:46.528 --> 00:03:49.905
"I'll drop Sid off at Monster Academy tomorrow after school.

56
00:03:49.906 --> 00:03:51.750
You can keep an eye on him."

57
00:03:51.751 --> 00:03:55.903
"Oh, boy!" Sid shouted. "This is going to be great!"

58
00:03:55.904 --> 00:04:00.686
"But I have volunteer stuff to do at the show," Ben moaned.

59
00:04:00.687 --> 00:04:04.451
Besides, he wanted to hang out with his friends.

60
00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.560
"Sid can help you with the duties," his mother said.

61
00:04:07.561 --> 00:04:09.446
"I'm sure he won't get in the way."

62
00:04:09.447 --> 00:04:10.169
"But—"

63
00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.047
Ben's father cut him off with a stern look.

64
00:04:13.048 --> 00:04:17.086
"A ghost who wants a pet needs to show responsibility, Ben.

65
00:04:17.087 --> 00:04:22.095
So you should certainly be able to take care of your little brother for a few hours without difficulty."

66
00:04:22.096 --> 00:04:32.072
Ben was trapped. "Okay," he said with a heavy sigh.

67
00:04:32.073 --> 00:04:37.803
When Ben arrived at Monster Academy the next day, he grinned at the unusual scene.

68
00:04:37.804 --> 00:04:41.157
As always, monsters were streaming into the school building.

69
00:04:41.158 --> 00:04:45.545
But today some of them had brought their pets with them.

70
00:04:45.546 --> 00:04:49.922
Mr. Freaky stood outside, blowing his noses.

71
00:04:49.923 --> 00:04:52.470
"Now, students. Remember what I said:

72
00:04:52.471 --> 00:04:55.950
This afternoon you'll have an opportunity to work with your pets.

73
00:04:55.951 --> 00:04:59.775
Until then, let's keep everything under control!"

74
00:04:59.776 --> 00:05:05.086
Ben looked around. Gaby had her giant albino shrew.

75
00:05:05.087 --> 00:05:07.618
A vampire had brought a spider.

76
00:05:07.619 --> 00:05:16.052
Jen had her singing slug, and Cleo was towing a pet jackal with a leash.

77
00:05:16.053 --> 00:05:19.427
"Lucky Deb," Ben thought as he gazed at the pets.

78
00:05:19.428 --> 00:05:22.510
She had a funny piranha-keet that she had taught to speak.

79
00:05:22.511 --> 00:05:24.394
"Wrawck!" the bird squawked.

80
00:05:24.395 --> 00:05:33.861
"Everything is totally under control!"
